WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.160 --> 00:00:01.535
- I think my mouth is crying.

00:00:01.535 --> 00:00:02.368
(laughter)

00:00:02.368 --> 00:00:04.028
(musical chimes)

00:00:04.028 --> 00:00:05.708
(fast-paced tempo)

00:00:05.708 --> 00:00:07.310
- I'm really looking forward
to this grilled cheese.

00:00:07.310 --> 00:00:08.567
I'm just looking forward to see

00:00:08.567 --> 00:00:11.483
what's inside this mysterious,
expensive sandwich.

00:00:11.483 --> 00:00:12.796
- I'm a little suspicious

00:00:12.796 --> 00:00:15.438
of the combination of something fancy

00:00:15.438 --> 00:00:18.574
with something that's
pretty cheap and standard.

00:00:18.574 --> 00:00:20.049
- I'm really interested to see

00:00:20.049 --> 00:00:21.787
what a fancy grilled cheese is like

00:00:21.787 --> 00:00:23.495
because I believe the best grilled cheese

00:00:23.495 --> 00:00:25.295
is just Kraft singles and bread.

00:00:25.295 --> 00:00:26.839
- I think grilled cheese should need

00:00:26.839 --> 00:00:28.264
to be sliced triangular.

00:00:28.264 --> 00:00:30.144
That's like an important
thing for me, and,

00:00:30.144 --> 00:00:33.465
you know, really, when it
comes out on the plate,

00:00:33.465 --> 00:00:35.636
if it's not sliced the way I want,

00:00:35.636 --> 00:00:37.573
I'm gonna be a little upset.

00:00:37.573 --> 00:00:39.616
- Just grab an iron, American cheese...

00:00:39.616 --> 00:00:40.603
- No (chuckles).

00:00:40.603 --> 00:00:42.193
- Two pieces of white bread...

00:00:42.193 --> 00:00:43.088
- Aaaa (gasps).

00:00:43.088 --> 00:00:44.020
- And just make that sandwich.

00:00:44.020 --> 00:00:45.166
- Then you go to, like, iron your clothes

00:00:45.166 --> 00:00:46.559
and you're gonna smell like bread.

00:00:46.559 --> 00:00:47.953
- That might be good, though.
- Bread and butter.

00:00:47.953 --> 00:00:49.308
That might be kinda hot,
like, you walk into a club,

00:00:49.308 --> 00:00:50.800
smell like a grilled cheese (laughs).

00:00:50.800 --> 00:00:51.803
- Oh my god.

00:00:51.803 --> 00:00:54.628
(rhythmic, upbeat tempo)

00:00:54.628 --> 00:00:58.320
- Hi, I'm Joe Calderone at
Serendipity 3 in New York City

00:00:58.320 --> 00:01:00.882
and we're here today to
make the Quintessential

00:01:00.882 --> 00:01:04.574
Grilled Cheese Sandwich, which
has the Guinness World Record

00:01:04.574 --> 00:01:07.685
as the most expensive
sandwich in the world.

00:01:07.685 --> 00:01:08.908
- [Clark] What makes it the Quintessential

00:01:08.908 --> 00:01:10.011
Grilled Cheese Sandwich?

00:01:10.011 --> 00:01:13.285
- Well, first we start with
this beautiful French Pullman

00:01:13.285 --> 00:01:15.862
bread that is baked with
Dom Perignon champagne.

00:01:15.862 --> 00:01:17.589
- No, shut up.
- Oh my gosh.

00:01:17.589 --> 00:01:20.320
- As you can see, it's flecked
with 23-karat edible gold.

00:01:20.320 --> 00:01:21.153
(gasps)

00:01:21.153 --> 00:01:23.566
What we're gonna do is take
a little white truffle butter

00:01:23.566 --> 00:01:26.805
and brush the bread, so when
we put it in our panini press,

00:01:26.805 --> 00:01:29.336
it gets a nice, crisp, great flavor.

00:01:29.336 --> 00:01:32.576
Then, we're gonna use the
crème de la crème of cheeses,

00:01:32.576 --> 00:01:35.234
which is called Caciocavallo
Podolico cheese.

00:01:35.234 --> 00:01:38.357
This is from Podolico
cattle in Southern Italy,

00:01:38.357 --> 00:01:41.237
of which there are only 25,000 of them.

00:01:41.237 --> 00:01:43.779
They graze on aromatic grasses.

00:01:43.779 --> 00:01:44.612
- Wow.

00:01:44.612 --> 00:01:47.236
- Such as wild strawberry and licorice

00:01:47.236 --> 00:01:49.372
and they only lactate in May and June.

00:01:49.372 --> 00:01:51.578
- Is that cheese similar
to another kind of cheese?

00:01:51.578 --> 00:01:54.689
- It's like a cross between
a manchego and a parmesan,

00:01:54.689 --> 00:01:57.279
but it melts really well for
a grilled cheese sandwich.

00:01:57.279 --> 00:02:00.977
This is San Marzano, an
African lobster tail bisque.

00:02:00.977 --> 00:02:04.379
- Ah, yes. How much does
one of these things cost?

00:02:04.379 --> 00:02:06.384
- The Quintessential Grilled Cheese here

00:02:06.384 --> 00:02:08.602
at Serendipity is 214 dollars.

00:02:08.602 --> 00:02:09.435
- Oh no.

00:02:09.435 --> 00:02:10.268
- Okay.

00:02:10.268 --> 00:02:12.282
(cash register chime)

00:02:12.282 --> 00:02:14.616
- Ade, you've never had lobster bisque

00:02:14.616 --> 00:02:16.752
and you also put ketchup
on your grilled cheese,

00:02:16.752 --> 00:02:19.492
so please, I'm asking
you, take the first bite.

00:02:19.492 --> 00:02:20.585
(gasping)

00:02:20.585 --> 00:02:22.118
- Oh my god he went right for the dip.

00:02:22.118 --> 00:02:23.845
(squealing)

00:02:23.845 --> 00:02:26.678
(classical music)

00:02:33.063 --> 00:02:34.375
- Amazing.

00:02:34.375 --> 00:02:35.443
- Okay, you're not dippin?

00:02:35.443 --> 00:02:37.080
- I'm gonna try my first...

00:02:37.080 --> 00:02:37.939
- Okay.

00:02:37.939 --> 00:02:38.787
- Non dip.

00:02:38.787 --> 00:02:40.261
- [Clark] Oh my god.

00:02:40.261 --> 00:02:42.087
(classical music)

00:02:42.087 --> 00:02:42.920
Mmm.

00:02:42.920 --> 00:02:43.753
- What do you feel?

00:02:43.753 --> 00:02:44.650
- I feel rich.

00:02:44.650 --> 00:02:46.603
All the flavors have some sort of savory,

00:02:46.603 --> 00:02:48.319
like salty quality, but they all

00:02:48.319 --> 00:02:49.982
have their own distinct characteristics.

00:02:49.982 --> 00:02:53.012
- The lobster bisque
it makes it obviously,

00:02:53.012 --> 00:02:55.346
now all the sudden you're
like eatin seafood,

00:02:55.346 --> 00:02:57.923
it's very different, but
it really, the flavors

00:02:57.923 --> 00:02:58.978
compliment each other.

00:02:58.978 --> 00:03:00.623
- Yeah, you have gold on your lips.

00:03:00.623 --> 00:03:01.981
(laughter)

00:03:01.981 --> 00:03:04.071
That is the most extra
thing I have ever seen.

00:03:04.071 --> 00:03:05.755
- I'm just gonna save it for later.

00:03:05.755 --> 00:03:09.230
- Okay, I'm just gonna try a gold flake.

00:03:09.230 --> 00:03:10.476
- It tastes...

00:03:10.476 --> 00:03:11.533
- Doesn't taste like anything.

00:03:11.533 --> 00:03:12.719
- Tastes like gold.

00:03:12.719 --> 00:03:14.774
- I'm sorry for whoever goes out with me.

00:03:14.774 --> 00:03:16.972
I can probably only
afford like one of these.

00:03:16.972 --> 00:03:19.630
You might have to get some
crushed ice and water.

00:03:19.630 --> 00:03:24.391
- I don't tend to spend 200
plus dollars on my meals,

00:03:24.391 --> 00:03:27.502
but I like to imagine a time when

00:03:27.502 --> 00:03:29.835
I'm just so freakin wealthy.

00:03:30.727 --> 00:03:33.432
- Grilled cheese is a comfort
food, but if I got let go

00:03:33.432 --> 00:03:35.510
from a job or I just needed
an ultimate pick-me-up,

00:03:35.510 --> 00:03:38.134
this is like, hey, you're
awesome, you're doin fine,

00:03:38.134 --> 00:03:40.595
you're worth it, so have
this great grilled cheese.

00:03:40.595 --> 00:03:43.416
Are you saying you're having
a bit of a cheese awakening?

00:03:43.416 --> 00:03:45.052
- That was very cheesy, yes.

00:03:45.052 --> 00:03:45.904
(laughter)

00:03:45.904 --> 00:03:46.860
- Oh yeah, you guys.

00:03:46.860 --> 00:03:47.693
- It's all Gouda.

00:03:47.693 --> 00:03:48.526
- These puns.

00:03:48.526 --> 00:03:51.359
(classical music)

